"""Row-by-row review table: EPA Level III unit -> PlantDex region, against the RECOVERED region names (PROPOSAL tooling).

Every one of the 85 units has an entry; make_mapping_v2.py fails on a missing or unknown unit, so nothing is silently assigned.

state:
  assigned       one region; the recovered name or plain geography decides it
  assigned-near  one region carried, and a named alternative is a defensible reading (a judgement about where a line runs)
  uncertain      evidence does NOT decide between the listed regions; `primary` is a carried best guess ONLY so a resolver has an
                 answer, and the resolver must surface the alternatives and never present it as settled
basis:
  NAME   decided by the wording of the owner's region name (a recovered fact) against the unit's name / EPA Level II group
  GEO    decided by my reading of the geography and vegetation; NOT verified against any floristic source, it is a reviewer opinion
  OWNER  cannot be decided from anything recovered; the owner's boundary rule is needed (see region-taxonomy.md s3)
`changed` records the v1 (assumed-name) assignment when v2 differs.
"""
